  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Linear Programming: the search line</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.4 (c): Find the gradient of the search line for a linear objective, the last vertex of the feasible region it touches, and the optimum value.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 8, Section 2.2 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: lines of equal cost as parallel lines, with the best line through the region, turned into a search line for a maximum or minimum, with new regions.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
